# 1. Who we are and what this policy covers

This policy explains how [Operator legal name] ("Naskun", "we", "us") collects, uses and protects your personal data when you use the Naskun app in Oman, the United Arab Emirates and Saudi Arabia. We are responsible for this processing; our contact details are at the end of this policy.

# 2. Data we collect

- Account data: name, email, phone number (optional), profile photo and sign-in method. With Google sign-in we receive that account's name, email and photo; with Sign in with Apple we receive your email (or an Apple private relay address if you choose to hide it) and your name if you share it. We never see your password; Firebase Authentication checks it.
- Guests without an account: a temporary anonymous identifier, used to protect the service and to count statistics without duplicates.
- Owner data: business name, booking phone, WhatsApp number, country, ownership proof document, the time you accepted the Owner Terms, verification status and any rejection reason.
- Place data: name, description, type, price, amenities, map location, area, photos and contact numbers, which become public when published.
- Photos you upload: we remove the location (GPS) data embedded in a photo on your device before uploading it; other technical data such as orientation, capture date and device model may remain.
- What you create: favorites, saved searches with their filters and alert setting, reviews (stars, tags, comment), reports (reason, description), ownership claims (message and documents), and support chat messages and images.
- Device and notification data: the app installation ID used to send notifications (Firebase Installation ID), platform, device language and app version, your notification preference, and your in-app notification history. On iPhone, notifications are delivered through Apple's push notification service.
- Usage data: opening a place page, tapping call, WhatsApp or directions, saving a favorite, searches by country and area, and technical measurements of distance calculation. These events carry ids, codes and counts only, never names, phone numbers or locations, and go to Firebase Analytics and our servers. Firebase Analytics may derive an approximate location (country or city) from your IP address. We do not use your device's advertising identifier and do not track you across other apps or websites.
- Crash reports: through Firebase Crashlytics, with an internal account id, account role, app version and language, never names, emails, phone numbers, messages or precise location. Google libraries built into the app, such as Google Maps and Google sign-in, collect technical diagnostic and performance data under their own policies.
- App integrity: Firebase App Check confirms that requests come from a genuine copy of the app; on iPhone it relies on Apple's App Attest and DeviceCheck.
- Administrative records: any suspension reason, internal team notes, and an admin action log holding ids only.
- On your device only: language, theme, chosen search country and an unsent support draft.

# 3. Location data

- We access your location only with your permission, asked when needed. You can refuse and choose a city or area yourself.
- We use location to detect your country, show the nearest places and calculate road distances.
- For distances, your location is sent to our servers, rounded to about 50 meters, then sent with the places' locations to Google's route service. We do not store your location or the distances on our servers permanently; distances are kept in your device's memory for up to 30 minutes.
- Country detection uses your phone's built-in location service, which may contact the platform provider.
- Tapping "Directions" opens Google Maps with the same starting point and the place as destination.
- A saved search stores the filters you chose, including the location you set for the search.

# 4. How we use data

- To run your account and the service: sign-in, email verification and password reset emails, showing and searching places, favorites, saved searches and reviews.
- To review places before publishing, verify owners and decide ownership claims.
- To moderate content, handle reports and prevent fraud and abuse.
- To send notifications about your account and activity, and to answer support requests.
- To show aggregated statistics to owners and the Naskun team, and to improve the app and fix crashes.
- To comply with the law and respond to lawful requests.

We process data to provide the service you asked for, for our legitimate interest in protecting and improving it, with your consent where consent is required (such as location and notifications), and to meet legal obligations, under [Applicable data protection laws]. We do not sell your personal data.

# 5. What others see and who can access your data

- Everyone: published places and their contact numbers, reviews with the writer's display name, and owners' replies.
- Owners: reviews of their places and aggregated statistics that do not identify who viewed or contacted. When you call or WhatsApp an owner, they see your number as that service shows it.
- The Naskun team: account data, ownership proofs and claim documents, reports and support chats, as needed for its work.
- Service providers: Google, as provider of Firebase, Google Maps and the route service, and Apple, as provider of notifications, Sign in with Apple and app integrity checks on iPhone, as the service requires.
- Authorities: where required by law, or to protect rights and safety.

# 6. Service providers and transfers outside your country

The app and its data are hosted on Google Firebase (sign-in, database, storage, cloud functions, messaging, analytics, crash reporting, app integrity and remote configuration), and we use Google Maps and Google's route service. Data is processed and stored on Google servers, including in the United States, outside your country and the GCC. We rely on [Safeguards for transfers abroad] for these transfers.

