- Anonymous guest identifiers: [Retention period for guest identifiers].
- Backups and server logs: [Retention period for backups and logs].

# 8. Deleting your account

You can delete your account yourself from "Account", then "Delete account", after confirming your identity. The same process applies when the Naskun team deletes an account. On deletion:

- Deleted: the account and sign-in, profile and photo, favorites, saved searches, notifications, devices registered for notifications, and the support chat and its images. If you sign in with Apple, we also revoke Naskun's link to your Apple account.
- Also deleted for owners: the business profile and ownership proof, drafts and never-published places with their photos, and claim documents; the owner's offers end.
- Hidden: every published place of a deleted owner, which becomes claimable by its rightful owner; pending requests are cancelled.
- Kept without your name: your reviews, stars and text, so places' ratings do not change, shown as "Deleted user"; your reports; and the history of your requests.
- Kept without personal data: an internal record that the account was deleted and the admin action log, both holding an internal id only, never your name, email or phone.

Deletion is permanent and cannot be undone. You may later create a new account with the same email.

# 9. Your rights and choices

- Access your data, learn how it is processed, and request a copy.
- Correct your data: edit your name, phone and photo in "Account", and ask support to correct anything else.
- Delete your account and its data directly in the app.
- Turn push notifications off, and withdraw location, notification or photo permissions in your phone's settings at any time.
- Withdraw consent, object to or ask to restrict certain processing, as the law allows.
- Complain to [Competent supervisory authority].

To exercise your rights, use the support chat or [Privacy email]. We will reply within [Response period]. We may need to verify your identity first.

# 10. Device permissions

- Location: to detect your country, show the nearest places and calculate distances.
- Notifications: requested when you turn notifications on, enable a saved-search alert, send a support message or submit a place for review, never just because you opened the app.
- Camera, photos and files: only when you choose to upload a profile photo, place photos, a support image, or a proof or claim document.

# 11. Security

Server-side access rules stop any account from reading or changing another's data, and App Check verifies requests. Ownership proofs, claim documents and support images are visible only to the account they belong to and the Naskun team. Temporary passwords created by the Naskun team are shown once and never stored. No protection is perfect, so keep your password secret.

# 12. Children

The app is not intended for anyone under [Minimum age], and we do not knowingly collect their data. If you learn that a child has created an account, contact us so we can delete it.

# 13. Changes to this policy

We may update this policy from time to time. The app shows its version number and last-updated date, and we will notify you in the app of material changes before they take effect.

